cus px-md"><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute -z-[1] rounded-[inherit] inset-[0.5px] cds-btn-squish"><span data-cds-part="paint" class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] transition-[background-color,box-shadow,color] duration-fast ease-out group-focus-visible/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] group-[[data-initial-focus]:focus]/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] bg-fill-primary group-hover/btn:bg-fill-primary-hover group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-primary-hover group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 ">Next</span></button></div></div></div><div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 !mt-0 border" style="border-radius: calc(var(--cds-radius) + 8px);"></div></div></div></div><div><div class="standard-markdown grid-cols-1 grid [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0 gap-3 [&amp;_&gt;_*:last-child]:mb-0 print:block print:[&amp;_&gt;_:where(:not(:first-child))]:mt-3 standard-markdown"><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal" dir="ltr"><strong>3. Demo video — don't push this to GitHub.</strong> Video files are large, and GitHub isn't built for hosting them (there are strict size limits and it makes your repo bloated). Here's the right way:</p></div></div><div data-find-omitted="" class="pl-[var(--msg-block-inset,0.5rem)] pt-4 pb-4"><div><div class="@container relative flex w-full flex-col overflow-hidden bg-surface-2 font-ui" style="border-radius: calc(var(--cds-radius) + 8px);"><div class="flex flex-col gap-sm p-xl"><div class="grid"><div class="col-start-1 row-start-1 flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-sm "><span class="text-title font-medium text-primary">1. Record your screen walking through the app</span><span class="text-body text-secondary">On Windows, press Win+G to open Xbox Game Bar (built-in, free, no install needed). Click the record button (or Win+Alt+R) to start recording your screen. Open your live Streamlit app link and walk through it on camera: sign up, log in, upload a food photo, show the detected foods + nutrition + total, then click History to show a saved entry. Keep it short — 2-4 minutes is plenty. Press Win+Alt+R again to stop.</span></div><div class="col-start-1 row-start-1 flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-sm invisible"><span class="text-title font-medium text-primary">2. Find your recorded video</span><span class="text-body text-secondary">The recording saves automatically to This PC &gt; Videos &gt; Captures. You can optionally add a short voiceover explaining what's happening as you click through — not required, but makes it clearer for your supervisor.</span></div><div class="col-start-1 row-start-1 flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-sm invisible"><span class="text-title font-medium text-primary">3. Upload to YouTube as Unlisted</span><span class="text-body text-secondary">Go to youtube.com, sign in, click the upload icon, select your video. IMPORTANT: set visibility to 'Unlisted' (not Public, not Private) — this means only people with the exact link can view it, it won't show up in search or your channel, but you can freely share the link.</span></div><div class="col-start-1 row-start-1 flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-sm invisible"><span class="text-title font-medium text-primary">4. Share the link with your supervisor</span><span class="text-body text-secondary">Once uploaded, copy the video link and send it directly to your sir — same way you send your daily WhatsApp updates. You can say something like: 'Sir, here's a demo video of the completed app: [link]. You can also try it live here: [your Streamlit Cloud link].'</span></div></div><div class="mt-auto grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] items-center gap-x-md gap-y-lg pt-md [grid-template-areas:&#39;dots_dots&#39;_&#39;toggle_nav&#39;] @[480px]:grid-cols-[auto_minmax(max-content,1fr)_auto] @[480px]:[grid-template-areas:&#39;dots_toggle_nav&#39;]"><div class="-my-1 mx-outset min-w-0 overflow-x-auto py-1 scroll-